executionContract.intendedBehavior:
moe.record_commit's MOE_CONTESTED_HELD line names the real release routes and says which sessions can leave a TOOL witness. The untouched remedy lists three routes:
- a one-shot Claude session of this task edits the path;
- a later session of this task that found the path clean at its pre-flight edits it while every contesting peer stays idle;
- the stale peer task is completed or archived.
The editing remedy says 'a one-shot Claude session of this task'. A fixed witness sentence follows the editing remedy whenever the line has an untouched or editing hold. A strict-only line is byte-identical to today's.

moe.get_commit_scope's peerDeclared entries gain activeTaskIds: the contributing tasks active by the peerActive rule, in id order (every contributor without since). editingTaskIds is a subset of activeTaskIds, and peerActive === (activeTaskIds.length > 0). docs/MCP_SERVER.md documents both.
